A DLL mod that adds a world-map minimap, a target panel with health, posture, status buildup and active effects, and timers for your own status effects. Fully configurable via its config file.

[size=4][b][color=#C0860A]I[/color][color=#CA9623]n[/color][color=#D4A63B]t[/color][color=#DDB654]r[/color][color=#E7C66D]o[/color][color=#F1D686]d[/color][color=#F1D686]u[/color][color=#E7C66D]c[/color][color=#DDB654]t[/color][color=#D4A63B]i[/color][color=#CA9623]o[/color][color=#C0860A]n[/color][/b][/size]
This mod adds a minimap at the top-right corner of the screen and a target stats panel right below it, inspired by [url=https://github.com/kubilaiswf/kubilaiswf-minimap]Minimap[/url] and [url=https://github.com/samjviana/souls_vision]Souls Vision[/url]. It also displays other useful information such as effect timers, the in-game time and your death count, and moves your own status buildup bars to the top-left so they are easier to see, making your gameplay experience smoother.

[size=4][b][color=#C0860A]F[/color][color=#CF9F31]e[/color][color=#DFB858]a[/color][color=#EED17F]t[/color][color=#EED17F]u[/color][color=#DFB858]r[/color][color=#CF9F31]e[/color][color=#C0860A]s[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Round minimap with the game's world map for the Lands Between, underground areas, dungeons and the Land of Shadow.[/*]
[*]Shows found Sites of Grace, points of interest, your placed beacons, summoned spirits, co-op partners and the locked-on enemy using the game's own map icons.[/*]
[*]Shows markers from [url=https://github.com/VirusAlex/ERR-MapForGoblins-DLL]Map for Goblins[/url] when that mod is installed.[/*]
[*]Option to reveal the whole map or only the areas uncovered by your map fragments.[/*]
[*]Option to rotate the minimap with the camera or keep north at the top.[/*]
[*]Optional compass letters, walked-path trail, in-game clock and death counter.[/*]
[*]Optional auto-hide in caves and dungeons or during boss fights.[/*]
[*]Hotkeys to zoom the minimap in and out.[/*]
[*]Hotkey to hide and show the minimap and the target panel.[/*]
[*]Target panel showing the locked-on enemy's health, posture and status buildup bars, styled after the game's HUD.[/*]
[*]Countdown timers for active effects on both the locked-on enemy and your own status icons.[/*]
[*]Moves your own status buildup bars to the top-left under your status icons, compatible with [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/3419]The Convergence[/url].[/*]
[*]Optional in-game settings menu when [url=https://github.com/Flammrock/ERNativeUI]ERNativeUI[/url] is installed.[/*]
[*]Hotkey to reload the config file without restarting the game.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#C0860A]N[/color][color=#DBB24E]o[/color][color=#F6DE92]t[/color][color=#DBB24E]e[/color][color=#C0860A]s[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*]If another overlay mod causes loading problems, delay this mod's loading if your mod loader supports it, or set [b]LoadDelay[/b] (in milliseconds, e.g. 10000) in the General section of [i]JourneyHUD.toml[/i].[/*]
[*]Install [url=https://www.patreon.com/huutaiii/posts/erss-early-v5-1-114748623]ERSS[/url] through your mod loader, not in the game folder. With ModEngine3, also set [b]load_early = true[/b] for it.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#D93A2B]D[/color][color=#DB3E2F]i[/color][color=#DC4333]s[/color][color=#DE4738]c[/color][color=#E04B3C]l[/color][color=#E14F40]a[/color][color=#E35444]i[/color][color=#E55849]m[/color][color=#E65C4D]e[/color][color=#E86051]r[/color][color=#EA6555]:[/color] [color=#EB6959]O[/color][color=#ED6D5E]n[/color][color=#EE7162]l[/color][color=#F07666]y[/color] [color=#F27A6A]u[/color][color=#F37E6E]s[/color][color=#F58273]e[/color] [color=#F78777]i[/color][color=#F88B7B]n[/color] [color=#FA8F7F]o[/color][color=#FC9384]f[/color][color=#FD9888]f[/color][color=#FF9C8C]l[/color][color=#FD9888]i[/color][color=#FC9384]n[/color][color=#FA8F7F]e[/color] [color=#F88B7B]m[/color][color=#F78777]o[/color][color=#F58273]d[/color][color=#F37E6E]e[/color] [color=#F27A6A]w[/color][color=#F07666]i[/color][color=#EE7162]t[/color][color=#ED6D5E]h[/color] [color=#EB6959]E[/color][color=#EA6555]A[/color][color=#E86051]C[/color] [color=#E65C4D]d[/color][color=#E55849]i[/color][color=#E35444]s[/color][color=#E14F40]a[/color][color=#E04B3C]b[/color][color=#DE4738]l[/color][color=#DC4333]e[/color][color=#DB3E2F]d[/color][color=#D93A2B]![/color][/b][/size]

[size=4][b][color=#C0860A]I[/color][color=#CA9623]n[/color][color=#D4A63B]s[/color][color=#DDB654]t[/color][color=#E7C66D]a[/color][color=#F1D686]l[/color][color=#F1D686]l[/color][color=#E7C66D]a[/color][color=#DDB654]t[/color][color=#D4A63B]i[/color][color=#CA9623]o[/color][color=#C0860A]n[/color][/b][/size]

Any DLL mod loader works, e.g. [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/117]Elden Mod Loader[/url], [url=https://github.com/soulsmods/ModEngine2/releases]Mod Engine 2[/url], [url=https://github.com/garyttierney/me3/releases]Mod Engine 3[/url].

[b]Option 1 - [url=https://github.com/soulsmods/ModEngine2/releases]Mod Engine 2[/url] (recommended)[/b]
[list=1]
[*]Download Mod Engine 2 from the link above and extract it into your game folder (the same folder as [i]eldenring.exe[/i]).[/*]
[*]Download this mod, then create a folder to hold it and its config file - for example, inside your game folder create a [b]natives[/b] folder.[/*]
[*]Open [b]config_eldenring.toml[/b] and edit [b]external_dlls = [ ][/b] to add the DLL, e.g.:
[code]external_dlls = [
    "natives\\JourneyHUD.dll",
][/code]
[/*]
[*]Launch the game using Mod Engine 2's launcher, [b]modengine2_launcher.exe[/b].[/*]
[/list]

[b]Option 2 - [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/eldenring/mods/117]Elden Mod Loader[/url][/b]
[list=1]
[*]Download Elden Mod Loader from the link above and extract it into your game folder.[/*]
[*]Download this mod and drag [b]JourneyHUD.dll[/b] and [b]JourneyHUD.toml[/b] into the [b]mods[/b] folder.[/*]
[*]Launch the game - the mod will be loaded automatically.[/*]
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#C0860A]C[/color][color=#D2A337]r[/color][color=#E4C165]e[/color][color=#F6DE92]d[/color][color=#E4C165]i[/color][color=#D2A337]t[/color][color=#C0860A]s[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Special thanks to [url=https://github.com/kubilaiswf]kubilaiswf[/url] ([url=https://github.com/kubilaiswf/kubilaiswf-minimap]kubilaiswf-minimap[/url]) for the world map archive reader, world coordinate conversion and minimap design.[/*]
[*]Thanks to [url=https://github.com/samjviana]samjviana[/url] ([url=https://github.com/samjviana/souls_vision]souls_vision[/url]) for the idea of displaying the locked-on enemy's health, posture and status buildup panel.[/*]
[*]Thanks to [url=https://github.com/soarqin]soarqin[/url] ([url=https://github.com/soarqin/EROverlay]EROverlay[/url]) for documenting how world map points and player beacons work.[/*]
[*]Thanks to [url=https://github.com/VirusAlex]VirusAlex[/url] and [url=https://github.com/soarqin]soarqin[/url] ([url=https://github.com/VirusAlex/ERR-MapForGoblins-DLL]Map for Goblins[/url]) for providing a public DLL API for map markers.[/*]
[*]Overlay built with [url=https://github.com/veeenu/hudhook]hudhook[/url] and [url=https://github.com/ocornut/imgui]Dear ImGui[/url].[/*]
[*]Game structures from [url=https://github.com/vswarte/fromsoftware-rs]fromsoftware-rs[/url].[/*]
[/list]

